  <content>
  <section><title>Lesson Narrative</title>
<para>This lesson focuses on the many ways that students will use information to write linear equations. Students will review writing linear equations given two points, a slope and a point, and the slope and \(y\)-intercept. Students will also become more comfortable using the point-slope form and slope-intercept form. Additionally, students will focus more on creating a table of values from a verbal description as well as using a table of values to then write a linear equation.</para>
<title>Learning Goals (Teacher Facing)</title>
<list>
  <item> Write linear equations given two points or a slope and point. </item>
  <item> Make a table of values to represent a verbal description. </item>
  <item> Write an equation from a table of values. </item>
</list>
<title>Learning Targets (Student Facing)</title>
<list>
  <item> Write equations from a point and slope. </item>
  <item> Write equations from two points. </item>
  <item> Write equations from a verbal description. </item>
  <item> Write equations from a table. </item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-textheavytable">
  <caption>
